.TH PARAM 1
.SH NAME
param \- print the values of the names of a source file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B param
.I file name ...
.br
.B param \-e
.I expr file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Param
reads the definitions of a source file of any kind,
.IR plicad (7):
its lines
.IB name " = " expr
and the definitions of the files its
.B include
lines name, in order.
Other lines are left alone.
It then prints the value of each
.IR name ,
or of the expression
.IR expr ,
one per line, a length in mm and an angle in degrees, to 12
significant digits.
.SH EXAMPLES
param box.sm wall depth
.br
param \-e '2*wall+1in' box.sm
.SH SEE ALSO
plicad(7)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
An unknown name, a faulty expression and a file that cannot be read
are refused, with the file and the line.
